# Quote Workflow — Break-If-Wrong

Underquoting is the failure the owner has actually suffered. **Fail closed.**

## Provenance (No Exceptions)
- Every money-bearing line carries `rate_source_id` → a `supplier_rm_quotes`, `machine_hour_rates`, `outsource_quotes`, or `owner_input` row. No source, no line.
- An estimate is labelled: `is_estimate = 1` plus a basis naming historical transactions or market trend. Unlabelled = bug.
- Sendability follows **attestation, not storage.** With `masterdata_enabled` (default on) the editor is `/masterdata`. A `source_kind='demo'` row is quotable only when `attested_by` is set and its value differs from the shipped seed.
- The model never derives a price from prose, memory, or "similar jobs".

## Hard Cells and Gates
- `revision`, `quantity`, `material` (grade + condition in one cell) are hard cells: each must be `confirmed` before `stage='send'` succeeds. They cannot be tagged `assumption`.
- `heat_treat`, `finish`, `gdt` may be tagged `assumption`. At send, an open assumption BLOCKS until the override stores the customer's exact master-data name (short name / alias refused).
- Stale raw-material basis (> 30 days) BLOCKS at send; the same override must also record the age Jarvis showed. Stale outsource is a WARN on the PDF.
- An empty delivery field BLOCKS at send. Jarvis never computes delivery.
- Labour-only orders carry no raw-material line; with-material always do.

## `quote_verify` and send
- Checks are `BLOCKER` or `WARN`. Any BLOCKER ⇒ `stop: true`; `quote_send` refuses to queue. Counting failures is not a severity model.
- Run proof against the stored `quote_revision`, not chat memory. The verified PDF is bound by sha256; `quote_send` re-hashes and refuses on drift.
- `quote_send` queues an Authorize card and never sets `sent: true`. The card shows total, currency, scope, rate sources, estimate flags, and a duplicate-delivery check.

The full decision context (manufacturing physics, floor freshness, blast radius, locked choices) lives in `docs/SYSTEM_TRUTH.md` §3 and §4. This file holds only the constraints an editor must not violate.
